    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e46123ed-d62a-3fdf-a460-31b7a4f76a88",
                "word": "nontheistic",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                        "entry_id": "e46123ed-d62a-3fdf-a460-31b7a4f76a88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not believing in any gods."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8962c88d-5670-4f74-8c58-74d1277f8d66",
                                "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                                "text": "The most influential contemporary school of non-theistic philosophers, the school of Comte, deny that either theism or atheism can be proved, and proscribe, with impartial rigour, all argument on either side..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e3fcbae-604e-4867-a0eb-f7d4c1b63372",
                                "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                                "text": "If the universe be regarded as self-existing, then men might hold to evolution, which is distinctly non-theistic, if not atheistic, not requiring a God for the reason that it is founded on the assumption that the possibility and potency and promise of all things reside in matter as matter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61dbecc9-1c4f-48e7-8c5d-12fd737830a3",
                                "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                                "text": "But to determine the position and worth of a religion, whether theistic or non-theistic, it is indispensable that we have some notion of what religion is in itself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7995bf60-ef89-44f2-b89d-4af8c841e64e",
                                "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                                "text": "Thus what he called \"natural religion\" must not be confused with modern brands of naturalistic or nontheistic religion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "464caf41-f536-445a-a2fd-fd9098fc4d69",
                                "sense_id": "c09fc4f3-99a1-38fe-bf2d-f186fb10e058",
                                "text": "The nontheistic tradition of Buddhism generally takes the view that people (with each other's help) can liberate themselves."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
